### 2.5. Use HTTPS / enforce secure cookies

When you start serving the app behind a reverse proxy (NGINX, CloudFront, etc.) make sure TLS is terminated there. In the Express layer you can force HTTPS for any direct access:

```js
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  // Redirect HTTP → HTTPS
  app.enable('trust proxy'); // needed if behind a load balancer
  app.use((req, res, next) => {
    if (req.secure) {
      return next();
    }
    res.redirect(`https://${req.headers.host}${req.originalUrl}`);
  });
}
```

*Why?* Handles **A07** (authentication failures via session hijacking) and **A05: Security Misconfiguration**.

